      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s first store opened in 1833, soon followed by a blacksmith, grocery, and shoemaker, marking the start of its early commerce.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green_Hill%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Green Hill sits on a rise overlooking Little Pine Creek, about 13 miles northeast of Williamsport and just south of Otterbein.",
